{
  "schema": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Standard looks and sizes for equipment drawn on unit models. These are DEFAULTS: a starting point that is",
    "then checked against each Mek's own artwork. A chassis recipe adjusts them with its weaponOverrides list",
    "(for example the Marauder's long dorsal autocannon) instead of editing this file.",
    "The look comes from the weapon's TYPE, read from its catalog family and name, never from its tonnage.",
    "All lengths and widths are model units at scale 1 and are multiplied by the recipe's weaponScale, so a",
    "light Mek's weapons are smaller than an assault Mek's while the proportions between weapons stay fixed.",
    "Rules are tried in order and the first match wins. Every matching modifier is then applied in order.",
    "A name is a case-insensitive regular expression searched in the catalog's display name.",
    "Segment positions (from, to) are measured back from the muzzle; a negative value lies beyond it.",
    "Every barrel has four standard protrusions, given as a share of its full length: recessed is a port flat",
    "against the armor, then short, medium and long. Arms default to long. Elsewhere a weapon uses its",
    "torsoProtrusion when it has one, else long. A recipe chooses per location with its protrusion map,",
    "or per weapon with a protrusion entry in weaponOverrides.",
    "A launcher mounts either way up: horizontal is wider than tall, vertical is the same grid turned on its",
    "side. A recipe sets missileOrientation for the whole Mek or per location; the default is horizontal.",
    "Tip colors: red for lasers, blue for PPCs only, green for TAG, orange for plasma and TSEMP.",
    "Multi-barrel weapons use the gatling look. A rotary autocannon is a ring of six thin round barrels; a HAG",
    "is four square Gauss rails in a two-by-two block, in three weights: HAG/20 light, HAG/30 medium, HAG/40 heavy.",
    "An anti-missile system is a small gatling gun on a compact housing, like a naval close-in weapon system;",
    "the laser version keeps the housing and shows a single red lens instead.",
    "HARD POINT CONVENTIONS. A weapon follows the limb it is mounted on: when an arm is posed hanging down,",
    "the recipe's socketAim gives that hard point a direction so the barrel runs along the forearm instead of",
    "jutting out at a right angle. Leg weapons always ride just below the hip, like a low-slung belt: the",
    "generator lifts them to hip height minus five unless the recipe supplies beltSockets. Jump jets stay put:",
    "in the calves, at the back. Weapons sharing a location are laid out inside that location's mounting area",
    "(recipe key mountAreas, else a default around the hard point); Java UnitModelMountArea performs the live fit.",
    "A searchlight is a box with a pale lens filling its face, exported as a separate optional equipment module.",
    "Runtime presence comes from mounted equipment or an explicit external housing; never bake it into the body.",
    "ARM ACTUATORS decide how an arm weapon looks, per variant. With a hand actuator the weapon rides on the",
    "forearm. With the hand missing it attaches at the wrist. With the lower arm missing it attaches at the",
    "elbow. A body function tags optional arm parts LA@elbow, LA@forearm, LA@wrist, LA@hand (and RA@...), and the",
    "recipe gives an armSockets entry per form; socketBanks may be keyed by form, e.g. LA@wrist:ppc."
  ],
